## Culture of mastocytoma cells
The autonomous malignant mastocytoma subline L138C3-1Oa from Balb/c mouse-derived bone marrow mast cells [26] was kindly provided by Dr L. Hultner (Minchen). The cells were maintained in RPMI 1640 medium supplemented with $2\mathrm{mM}$ $\mathbf{L}$ -glutamine, $20\%$ heat-inactivated fetal calf serum, $100\:\mathrm{IU/ml}$ penicillin/streptomycin, and $100\upmu\mathbf{M}$ $\alpha$ -thioglycerol, in a humidified incubator $5\%$ $\mathbf{CO}_{2}$ ， $37^{\circ}\mathrm{C})$ [26].
## Preparation and characterization of plasma membrane vesicles
Plasma membrane vesicles from mastocytoma cells were prepared using hypotonic lysis of the cells [8, 27]. The cells $\bar{(3\times10^{9})}$ were harvested from the cell culture by centrifugation ( ${1200\times g}$ ， $10\mathrm{min}$ ， $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ ）and washed twice in ice-cold phosphate-buffered saline( $150\mathrm{mM}\mathrm{NaCl}$ ， $5\mathrm{mM}$ sodium phosphate $\mathrm{pH}7.4\AA.$ ）followed by centrifugation at $1200\times g$ ·1 The resulting cell pellet (about $5\mathrm{ml}$ ）was diluted 40-fold with hypotonic buffer ( $\mathrm{70.5~mM}$ sodium phosphate $\mathsf{p H}7.0$ $\mathbf{0.1\mM}$ “EGTA） supplemented with protease inhibitors $(0.1\ \mathrm{mM}$ $\mathbf{PhMeSO}_{2}\mathbf{F}$ ， $2.8\upmu\mathrm{M}$ E64， $1~\upmu\mathbf{M}$ leupeptin, and $0.3\upmu\mathrm{M}$ aprotinin) and gently stirred on ice for $1.{\bar{5}}\mathrm{h}$ The cell lysate was subsequently centrifuged at $100000\times g$ for $40\mathrm{min}$ at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ . The pellet was resuspended in $20\mathrm{ml}$ hypotonic buffer and homogenized with a Braun potter S 886 ( $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ $500\mathrm{rpm}$ 30 strokes, 2 strokes/min). The resulting homogenate was diluted with incubation buffer $250\mathrm{mM}$ sucrose, $10\mathrm{m}\mathbf{M}$ Tris/HCl pH 7.4) and centrifuged at $12000\times g$ for $10\mathrm{min}$ at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ . The resulting postnuclear supernatant was stored on ice and the corresponding pellet was resuspended in $20~\mathrm{ml}$ incubation buffer supplemented with the protease inhibitors, again homogenized by 20 strokes (potter S 886, $500\mathrm{rpm}$ .2 strokes/min, $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C})$ ）and centrifuged ( $12000\times g$ ,10 min, $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C})$ ： Both postnuclear supernatants were combined and centrifuged at $100000\times g$ for $40\mathrm{min}$ at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ . Subsequently the pellets were resuspended in $20~\mathrm{ml}$ incubation buffer and manually homogenized by 5O strokes with a tight-fitting Dounce B (glass/glass) homogenizer on ice. After dilution with $10\mathrm{ml}$ incubation buffer, this crude membrane fraction was layered over $38\%$ sucrose in $\mathsf{5}\mathrm{mM}$ Hepes/KOH $\mathrm{pH}7.4$ and centrifuged at $280000\times g$ for $^{2\mathrm{~h~}}$ at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ in a swing-out rotor. The interphases were collected, diluted in $20\mathrm{ml}$ incubation buffer and again homogenized with a tight-fitting Dounce B (glass/ glass) homogenizer (30 strokes). This suspension was then centrifuged at $100000\times g$ for $40\mathrm{min}$ at $4^{\circ}\bar{\mathbf{C}}$ and the resulting pellets were diluted in $1~\mathrm{ml}$ incubation buffer. Vesicles were formed by passing the suspension 20 times through a 27- gauge needle. The membrane vesicles were frozen and stored in liquid nitrogen. The protein concentration was determined according to Lowry et al. [28].
The resulting membrane vesicles showed $\mathrm{Na^{+}/K^{+}}$ -ATPase activity [29], as a marker of the plasma membrane, with enrichment factors of $15-30$ -fold as compared to the original cell homogenate. We observed moderate contamination from endoplasmic reticulum indicated by NADPH-cytochrome $\boldsymbol{c}$ reductase [30] which was $1.8\mathrm{-}3$ -fold enriched relative to the homogenate. $N\mathrm{.}$ -Acetylglucosamine :UDP-galactosyltransferase [31, 32] as a Golgi apparatus marker, was $_{3-5}$ -fold enriched relative to the homogenate. Succinate dehydrogenase activity [33], as mitochondrial marker, was below the detection limit. Ultrastructural examination of the membrane vesicle fractions by electron microscopy revealed predominantly closed vesicles of various sizes $(\bar{0}.1-0.7\upmu\mathrm{m})$ and only few open membrane sheets. Cell organelles and non-membranous protein aggregates were not observed.
## Vesicle transport studies
Transport of $\mathrm{[^{3}H]L T C_{4}}$ was measured by use of a rapid filtration apparatus (Millipore Corp.) using nitrocellulose filters $(0.2\upmu\mathrm{m}$ pore size) soaked in incubation buffer ( $250\mathrm{mM}$ sucrose, $10\mathrm{mM}$ Tris/HC1 $\mathrm{pH}7.4\AA,$ . Membrane vesicles were quickly thawed at $37^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ shortly before use and stored on ice.
CsA, PSC 833, and MK 571 were prepared as $10~\mathrm{mM}$ stock solutions in $100\%$ ethanol and stored at $-20^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ .The final dilution of the inhibitors in incubation buffer was performed on the day of the experiments and kept at $37^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for the time of the experiment to achieve better solubility of the drugs. The final ethanol concentration never exceeded $0.5\%$ . In the control experiments without inhibitors an appropriate dilution of ethanol was added to the incubation medium to control any effects of the solvent. ATP-dependent uptake of $[\mathrm{^{3}H}]\mathrm{LTC_{4}}$ into plasma membrane vesicles of mastocytoma cells was measured as described [8]  with the following modifications. After preincubation of the reaction mixture C $10~\mathrm{mM}$ Tris/HC1 $\mathsf{p}\bar{\mathsf{H}}7.4$ ， $206{\mathrm{mM}}$ sucrose, $\mathbf{4\mM}$ ATP, 10 mM $\mathbf{MgCl}_{2}$ $10\ \mathrm{{\bar{mM}}}$ creatine phosphate, $100\upmu\mathrm{g/ml}$ creatine kinase) containing varying concentrations of $\mathrm{[^{3}H]L T C_{4}}$ ， the incubation was started at $37^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ by addition of the membrane vesicle suspension ( $50\upmu\mathrm{g}$ protein). The final volume was $110\upmu\mathrm{l}$ . $20\mathrm{-}\upmu\bar{1}$ samples were taken at the indicated times (up to $3\:\mathrm{min}$ ）and diluted in $1~\mathrm{ml}$ ice-cold incubation buffer. The diluted samples were filtered immediately through the presoaked nitrocellulose filters and rinsed twice with $5\mathrm{ml}$ incubation buffer. Filters were dissolved and radioactivity measured in a liquid scintillation counter. In control experiments, ATP was replaced by an equal concentration of ${5^{\prime}}\mathrm{AMP}$ or, in some experiments, by adenosine $5^{\prime}{-}[\beta,\gamma$ -methylene]triphosphate $(\mathrm{Ado}P P[\mathrm{CH}_{2}]P)$ . Uptake rates were calculated by subtracting the corresponding values in the presence of ${5^{\prime}}\mathrm{A}\mathrm{\bar{M}P}$ or $\mathrm{Ado}P P[\mathrm{CH}_{2}]P$ from those in the presence of ATP.
