For taurocholate extraction, the labeled membranes were incubated in incubation buffer supplemented with $1\mathrm{mM}$ EDTA and $2\%$ sodium taurocholate for $30\mathrm{min}$ at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ and centrifuged at $100000\times g$ for $90\mathrm{min}$ [36,37]. The pellet was washed with taurocholate-containing buffer.
The resulting membrane pellets were dissolved in a buffer containing $63~\mathrm{mM}$ Tris/HC1 $\mathtt{p H}6.8$ $10\%$ glycerol, $5\%$ SDS, $5\%$ 2-mercaptoethanol, and $0.001\%$ bromophenol blue (sample buffer) [38] for SDS/PAGE, using a $15\%$ acrylamide gel, or the same buffer supplemented with $5\mathbf{M}$ urea when $7.5\%$ acrylamide gels containing $5\mathbf{M}$ urea were used. SDS/PAGE was performed using vertical gel slabs $(200{\times}140{\times}1.7\ \mathrm{mm})$ at $15^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ 、 After electrophoresis and staining with Coomassie brilliant blue R-250, gels were cut into slices of $2\mathrm{mm}$ thickness, dissolved in $0.5{\mathrm{ml}}$ tissue solubilizer and the radioactivity was measured in a liquid scintillation counter [34, 35, 39].
## Isoelectric focussing and two-dimensional electrophoresis
Labeled and taurocholate-extracted membranes $(300~\upmu\up g$ protein) were solubilized in $20\upmu10\%$ SDS and diluted fivefold with IEF sample buffer containing $2\%$ Chaps, $1\%$ Triton X-100， $100\mathrm{mM}$ dithiothreitol, $^{9\mathrm{{M}}}$ urea, $2.5\%$ Bio-Lyte $3/10,1\%$ Bio-Lyte $4/6$ ,and $1\%$ Bio-Lyte 8/10. The composition of the gel for IEF was $6\%$ acrylamide, $10\mathbf{M}$ urea, $5\%$ Bio-Lyte 3/10, $1.5\%$ Bio-Lyte $4/6$ ， $1.5\%$ Bio-Lyte 8/10, $2\%$ Chaps, and $1\%$ Triton $X{-}100$ . The catholyte was $50\mathrm{mM}$ NaOH and the anolyte was $50\mathrm{mM}$ ${\bf H}_{3}{\bf P O}_{4}$ . After an initial $^{1\mathrm{~h~}}$ of prefocussing of the gel, focussing was performed at constant voltage of $500\mathrm{v}$ for a total of $10\mathrm{kV/h}$ . For determination of radioactivity or of $\mathrm{\ttpH}$ values the gels were cut into $5\mathrm{-mm}$ pieces. Intact IEF gels were used for the separation in the second dimension by SDS/PAGE using a $15\%$ or $7.5\%$ $(5\mathbf{M}$ urea) resolving gel, and the SDS/PAGE sample buffer system with $1\%$ agarose. After silver staining, the gels were cut into $5\times5-\mathrm{mm}^{2}$ pieces and the radioactivity was measured in a liquid scintillation counter.
## Deglycosylation by peptide N-glycosidase F
The labeled and taurocholate-extracted membrane pellets $(200\upmu\mathrm{g}$ protein) were suspended in $20\upmu10\up m\up M$ Tris/HCI $\mathrm{pH}7.4$ $1\%$ SDS, and incubated at $95^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ . After 2 min of incubation, the samples were diluted 1O-foid with a buffer containing $20\mathrm{mM}$ sodium phosphate $\mathrm{pH}7.4$ ， $5\mathrm{mM}$ EDTA, $0.2\mathrm{mM}\mathrm{NaN_{3}}$ ，and $0.5\%$ Nonidet P-40, and incubated again for $2\mathrm{min}$ at $95^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ . Then these samples were cooled to $20^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ The deglycosylation was started by addition of $_{5\mathrm{~U~}}$ peptide $\mathbf{N}$ -glycosidase $\boldsymbol{\mathrm{~F~}}$ and incubation was performed at $3\bar{7}^{\circ}\bar{\mathbf{C}}$ for $24\mathrm{{\bar{h}}}$ Control incubations were performed under the same conditions without the enzyme. After dilution with $300\upmu\mathrm{l}$ of $10\mathrm{mM}$ Tris/HC1 $\mathrm{pH}7.4$ ， the samples were concentrated by centrifugation in a Centricon-1O filter tube to one third of the volume which was then lyophilized. The lyophilisates were suspended in $30\upmu\mathrm{l}$ SDS/PAGE sample buffer and subjected to SDS/PAGE.
